From: Octo <180629317+OctoAlgo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 14:26:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 07/11] the natives hook finds its two call sites by byte
 pattern (exactly once in the executable sections)

The NATIVE opcode's call (lea rcx,[rsp+disp32]; vzeroupper; call r15) and the by-ID call (lea rcx,[rsp+28h];
lea r14,[rbx+disp32]; lea rdi,[rbx+disp32]; call [rax]) were fixed RVAs of 1.0.2.1 with a byte check; now each is
a pattern with its displacements open, searched in the image's executable sections, used only when it occurs
exactly once, and the stubs take the displacements found. The executable-hash gate stays. Host tests: the
patterns, and (with VICTORY_TITLE_EXE) both occur once in the 1.0.2.1 executable at +0x3de7503 / +0x3de2331.

